From 957f7b17b9da876c46079b2097a8055910b0faa8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Naresh Solanki <naresh.solanki.2011@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 23:31:12 +0530
Subject: net: dsa: add an 802.1Q-based tagger for MediaTek switches

tag_8021q-based tagging for MT7530-family switches as an alternative to
the MediaTek special tag (mtk-8021q, modelled on tag_vsc73xx_8021q): the
CPU port carries standard 802.1Q tags, with tag_8021q's per-port
standalone VIDs and per-bridge VIDs identifying the source port or
bridge. A MAC-side offload engine that only parses 802.1Q, such as the
SF19A2890 GMAC's NAT engine, can then see the frames.

Ports in a bridge use the bridge VID, standalone ports their own.

The tagger provides its own flow_dissect: the generic one skips
needed_headroom bytes as if the tag were still in the data, but a
conduit with rx-vlan-offload has already stripped it, so every flow
hashed alike and RPS put all receive work on one CPU.

Signed-off-by: Naresh Solanki <naresh.solanki.2011@gmail.com>
